                        "entry_id": "ee5e7086-d0af-38f8-a87e-d2da939e8cb2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "мифол. в греческой мифологии — пища богов"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "42010ebd-4908-38f3-9c9f-5e366c4efaa5",
                        "entry_id": "ee5e7086-d0af-38f8-a87e-d2da939e8cb2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ботан. налёт мицелия некоторых сумчатых грибов, выстилающий в древесине ходы, в которых живут личинки жуков-короедов"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d82cc5dd-c579-3823-97aa-ecd4a5337f6b",
                        "entry_id": "ee5e7086-d0af-38f8-a87e-d2da939e8cb2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ботан. травянистое растение семейства астровых (лат. Ambrosia)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e25b7fb-d111-4e90-bfda-7c68f56ca4ed",
                                "sense_id": "d82cc5dd-c579-3823-97aa-ecd4a5337f6b",
                                "text": "Пыльца амброзии может вызывать сенную лихорадку."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5c89a015-6d9b-3d3d-8428-7e0de2f3bc20",
                        "entry_id": "ee5e7086-d0af-38f8-a87e-d2da939e8cb2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., шутл. вкусная, изысканная пища"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ec95803-a5e7-4e72-a70b-c57277cfc7b1",
                                "sense_id": "5c89a015-6d9b-3d3d-8428-7e0de2f3bc20",
                                "text": "Пациенту дают выпить стакан глюкозы, а поскольку недостаток сахара ощущается буквально каждой клеточкой души и тела, первый глоток кажется почти что амброзией."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3282ae2b-7669-43df-a6d5-61379569b0ae",
                        "source_entry_id": "ee5e7086-d0af-38f8-a87e-d2da939e8cb2",
                        "source_sense_description": "мифическая пища богов",
                        "target_lang_word": "ambrosia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ambrosia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8ba0b21c-fe71-3695-a077-788bc19274c6",
                                        "entry_id": "dcb3c040-2ff6-398f-89a7-57e13d6dc927",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The food of the gods, thought to confer immortality."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Greek",
                                            "Roman",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f802fb1b-f466-428a-bab1-d90ef38aa15d",
                                                "sense_id": "8ba0b21c-fe71-3695-a077-788bc19274c6",
                                                "text": "He had a most intense admiration of female loveliness, and looked upon woman as a kind of super-angelic being, whose food should be the ambrosiæ and nectar of the gods, and whose garments the spotless white of vestal purity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3d666c75-0051-3122-82e0-5c37bc8a26fb",
                                        "entry_id": "dcb3c040-2ff6-398f-89a7-57e13d6dc927",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The anointing-oil of the gods."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Greek",
                                            "Roman",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a4474581-d8e4-3609-a9f2-2cb7be489a50",
                                        "entry_id": "dcb3c040-2ff6-398f-89a7-57e13d6dc927",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any food with an especially delicious flavour or fragrance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "39afb41f-3307-393f-ba90-bf51acbd5036",
                                        "entry_id": "dcb3c040-2ff6-398f-89a7-57e13d6dc927",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anything delightfully sweet and pleasing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23b5af66-e129-4e9f-be99-a9cce7a7a639",
                                                "sense_id": "39afb41f-3307-393f-ba90-bf51acbd5036",
                                                "text": "A favorite. It’s refreshing now and will evolve into golden ambrosia with age. […] The dessert wines of the Loire Valley and AJsace also deserve recognition. From the Anjou area of the Loire come the ambrosiae of Savennières, Bonnezeaux, and Quarts de Chaume."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b59d1437-dde1-3c29-b516-cd6b8827cf47",
                                        "entry_id": "dcb3c040-2ff6-398f-89a7-57e13d6dc927",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An annual herb historically used medicinally and in cooking, Dysphania botrys."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1829ee62-eb27-33a7-878c-d2054d246d85",
                                        "entry_id": "dcb3c040-2ff6-398f-89a7-57e13d6dc927",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mixture of nectar and pollen prepared by worker bees and fed to larvae."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b7db9e14-1159-3a3c-aec3-42071485ffc9",
                                        "entry_id": "dcb3c040-2ff6-398f-89a7-57e13d6dc927",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any fungus of a number of species that insects such as ambrosia beetles carry as symbionts, \\\"farming\\\" them on poor-quality food such as wood, where they grow, providing food for the insect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "59e01e01-b00c-3982-a179-4d5b4a09ca9f",
                                        "entry_id": "dcb3c040-2ff6-398f-89a7-57e13d6dc927",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dessert originating in the Southern United States made of shredded coconuts and tropical fruits such as pineapples and oranges; some recipes also include ingredients such as marshmallow and cream."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c4c54c8a-fecd-394d-bfd1-60fe89e400db",
                                        "entry_id": "dcb3c040-2ff6-398f-89a7-57e13d6dc927",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A plant of the genus Ambrosia."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ca719e3-827d-4ecf-8add-9d2714480724",
                                                "sense_id": "c4c54c8a-fecd-394d-bfd1-60fe89e400db",
                                                "text": "Their disease does not appear before August. At this time, throughout the entire United States one could say, not only in every field, in every meadow and in every forest, but even in the largest cities, there blooms the ambrosiæ, which are commonly known as ragweed; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46055d2e-fdd6-461b-8c58-92ade96c3ebb",
                                                "sense_id": "c4c54c8a-fecd-394d-bfd1-60fe89e400db",
                                                "text": "Fig. 1.—Spiculated pollens of ragweeds (ambrosias) low in protein. […] In the cocklebur (Xanthium americanum) and the rough wild elder (Iva ciliata), the spicules are shorter, being 0.7 and 0.5 microns, and the reaction is proportionately less active than with the ragweeds (ambrosias). […] While the grass pollens have so light a coat that they are frequently crushed in the ordinary process of mounting, the ragweed (ambrosias) pollen grains resist pressure between two glass slides carried to the point of crushing the glass."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "623b83bf-4615-4a6d-aa76-c41257b45be0",
                                                "sense_id": "c4c54c8a-fecd-394d-bfd1-60fe89e400db",
                                                "text": "Dr. William Scheppergrell,^([sic – meaning Scheppegrell]) in Public Health Reports, states that the common and giant ragweeds (ambrosias), which are the principal causes of hay fever in the Eastern States, do not grow so abundantly in the West, and that the pollens of other plants, notably the wormwoods (artemisias), are the exciting causes of hay fever in the Pacific and Mountain States. […] [quoting Scheppegrell] The most important hay-fever weeds of the Pacific and Mountain States, and which give the most severe reaction, are the wormwoods (artemisias). While their pollen is not produced in the same profusion as that of the ragweeds (ambrosias), they give a marked hay-fever reaction which in some species is five times as active as that of the ragweed (ambrosia)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "829268ec-c13a-43e6-a7b2-d74a0cc3f5f3",
                                                "sense_id": "c4c54c8a-fecd-394d-bfd1-60fe89e400db",
                                                "text": "Section G: The Collector’s corner, Mrs. J. R. Cowan, blue, for her ambrosiae."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d338fb7-8b29-4c25-8b1b-8574fbc1290a",
                                                "sense_id": "c4c54c8a-fecd-394d-bfd1-60fe89e400db",
                                                "text": "Once again there can be heard throughout the eastern part of the country the stacatto^([sic]) sneezing, the hacking cough and the stuffy head of the hay fever patient, for ragweed season is upon us. As it does each year, about the fifteenth of August, plants of the group called ambrosiae spread their pollens to the wind and the misery begins."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef0d4300-e44e-431b-9605-4a30df55da27",
                                                "sense_id": "c4c54c8a-fecd-394d-bfd1-60fe89e400db",
                                                "text": "The ambrosias [ragweeds] are not only very harmful competitors of plants, but they also are dangerous vectors of allergic illnesses of man."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8853910-0791-4a7f-bb6b-92e324b3c520",
                                                "sense_id": "c4c54c8a-fecd-394d-bfd1-60fe89e400db",
                                                "text": "To the west, perennial ragweed (A. psilostachya) and additional species including perennial slender ragweed (A. confertiflora) and annual bur ragweed (A. acanthocarpa) are prominent in the Great Plains and Great Basin areas, while canyon ragweed (A. ambrosioides), rabbit bush (A. deltoidea), and burroweed (A. dumosa) are ragweeds of southwestern deserts. Several of these species previously were classified in the genus Franseria (as “false ragweeds”); however, they appear to be valid ambrosias with respect to both form and pollen allergens."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78539246-ab24-4c58-ad12-db79ac5c21d7",
                                                "sense_id": "c4c54c8a-fecd-394d-bfd1-60fe89e400db",
                                                "text": "Sunflowers grace most of the continental United States with a lush, vibrant beauty. But not the ambrosiae. These plants—also called western ragweed—populate the sprawling southwestern flatlands of the Mojave, the Sonoran, and the Great Basin deserts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6488bcb0-b2ea-417b-a0c9-7aba5fd76775",
                        "source_entry_id": "ee5e7086-d0af-38f8-a87e-d2da939e8cb2",
                        "source_sense_description": "мифическая пища богов",
                        "target_lang_word": "ambroisie",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ambroisie",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7efc2167-ae71-34a7-9f48-08b70fbcda0d",
                                        "entry_id": "9cb3f4cf-ddd1-3079-97fd-5c44879df7ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Nourriture d’un goût et d’un parfum délicieux qui était destinée aux divinités de l’Olympe et qui donnait l’immortalité à ceux qui en goûtaient."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2fad4264-4455-4961-b541-52b052fef078",
                                                "sense_id": "7efc2167-ae71-34a7-9f48-08b70fbcda0d",
                                                "text": "Le nectar et l’ambroisie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "887ad27e-097a-4685-b4f9-e20740117c3a",
                                                "sense_id": "7efc2167-ae71-34a7-9f48-08b70fbcda0d",
                                                "text": "— N’était-ce point satiété ? dit Blazius, car d’ambroisie même on se dégoûte, et les dieux viennent manger sur terre le pain bis des humains."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "580bf20d-49e3-30a9-8a9a-10e83243254b",
                                        "entry_id": "9cb3f4cf-ddd1-3079-97fd-5c44879df7ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chose exquise."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb8f0e61-4c94-45ea-886c-f94d4b822528",
                                                "sense_id": "580bf20d-49e3-30a9-8a9a-10e83243254b",
                                                "text": "On a tort peut-être d’aborder trop tôt Homère, Eschyle, Dante, Shakspeare, Goethe, et de s’éblouir les yeux, dès la jeunesse, de Phidias, de Léonard de Vinci, de Michel-Ange, de Raphaël, de Titien, de Rembrandt. Il ne reste plus à lire et à contempler que des œuvres inférieures, secondaires, médiocres ou franchement mauvaises, et cela, lorsque le goût formé est devenu superbe et dédaigneux ; commencer par l’ambroisie et finir par la panade, c’est triste ; mais qu’y faire ?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c97e9032-c884-44a2-aa05-ff001daf7d0d",
                                                "sense_id": "580bf20d-49e3-30a9-8a9a-10e83243254b",
                                                "text": "Tout en faisant oublier adroitement Nicolas, pour dissiper la méfiance dans cette âme naïve, Catherine y distillait superfinement l’ambroisie des compliments."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6f806f85-8e89-33f4-9428-50a62225ef65",
                                        "entry_id": "9cb3f4cf-ddd1-3079-97fd-5c44879df7ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Genre de plantes envahissantes de la famille des Astéracées, aux feuilles très découpées, dont plusieurs espèces produisent des pollens très allergisants."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf0b68fd-85c4-41e3-85ed-de747b1784ab",
                                                "sense_id": "6f806f85-8e89-33f4-9428-50a62225ef65",
                                                "text": "L’ambroisie à feuilles d’armoise Ambrosia artemisiaefolia ; genre Ambrosia du grec ambrosios, qui donne l’immortalité : allusion à l’odeur aromatique de plusieurs espèces (Coste)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f22d316-d7ed-4cd1-9439-919ce230ed5f",
                                                "sense_id": "6f806f85-8e89-33f4-9428-50a62225ef65",
                                                "text": "C’est le cauchemar des allergiques : l’ambroisie. Cette mauvaise herbe, qui ne ressemble à rien et qu’on appelle aussi « herbe à poux », est une véritable bombe allergène."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8714292f-649d-47fd-8e6e-e594534a2cf1",
                                                "sense_id": "6f806f85-8e89-33f4-9428-50a62225ef65",
                                                "text": "Chaque année, il y a des sécheresses, et celle de 2020 a été la pire, il n’y avait même pas d'ambroisie, encore moins d'herbe."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
